<header><p class="enc-kicker">Institution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Swedish Academy</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1786">1786</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/18th-century">18th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Swedish Academy was founded by King <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gustav-iii">Gustav III</a> in 1786 to promote the purity and strength of the Swedish language, on the model of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/academie-francaise">Académie française</a>. It has eighteen members elected for life and publishes a great dictionary and the official word list of Swedish. Since 1901 it has chosen the winners of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/nobel-prize">Nobel Prize</a> in Literature.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/swedish-academy.jpg" alt="Swedish Academy" width="320" height="312" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Swedish Academy · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Svenska_Academien_seal.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
